# The credential lives here, and so does the choice of credential FORM
# (a plain value, or a secret URI needing an out-of-tree resolver).
# Neither belongs on a remote.
.env
!.env.example

# Runtime state the daemon writes into the workspace.  NOT `.jaato/`
# wholesale — the profiles under `.jaato/profiles/` are the deliverable,
# and a blanket ignore silently ships a clone with no profiles at all
# and a validate that finds nothing to check.
.jaato/logs/
.jaato/sessions/
.jaato/.artifact_tracker.json
# Written by the daemon during a run (note the `generated_at` stamp),
# not authored here.
.jaato/templates/

.claude/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Artifacts a RUN produces.  The example writes these; they are outputs,
# not sources, and committing one would make a stale run look canonical.
chapter.md
snippets/
hostile-notes/
cascade-transcript.md
roster-seen.txt
BOUNDARY_BREACHED.txt
